WEBVTT

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:12.790
Kyou kara mieru yo chiisai hoshi

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.210
Terashitete ne mune no naka o

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.500
Naite waratte kagaiyaite

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.750
Udemakutte arukidasou

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.960
(Kitto alright nayamu wa go sign)

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.210
(Kichin to yarimashou)

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:34.580
Jiyuu sugiru tte nante fujiyuu nan deshou

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.920
Datte tokenai no yo

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.330
Rironchi jikkenchi spiral

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:43.420
Maido utedo katte mo

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.000
(Nani o tameshite mite mo)

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.670
Nengan kanatte shikuhakku

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.500
(Cheat ja nai yo life hack)

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.960
Harete ippo fumidaseru license

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.210
Kore kara ga hajimari

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:58.460
Kyou kara mieru yo chiisai hoshi

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.830
Terashitete ne mune no naka o

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:05.250
Naite waratte kagaiyaite

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.830
Shigoto no mae wa shinkokyuu

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:12.000
Hibike te o nobashita shintenchi

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.330
Yume wa kitto te no naka

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:18.750
Kitto dekiru original

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.460
Door o akete welcome de ikou

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.960
(Sore ja koko ga start)

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:27.460
(Kitto alright nayamu wa go sign)

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.880
(Kichin to yarimashou)

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:39.670
Delicious!

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.790
It's got a great scent too.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:45.330
I splurged a bit on the tea leaves.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.250
The salamander ingredients sold for
a high enough price,

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.420
so there's nothing wrong with
doing that now and again.

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:57.580
I really am glad to get the chance to
drink tea again with all of you like this.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.420
We couldn't go dying so lightly

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:03.330
when we still had so much more
of your delicious cooking to eat.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:08.880
Still, I hardly felt like I was still alive
until we confirmed it had been defeated.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.170
It's frozen, isn't it?

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.290
Yes, it's fine now.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.920
You fought a monster like that...?

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.080
Salamanders sure are crazy huge, aren't they?

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:25.920
No, I believe this is no ordinary specimen.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:30.210
Still, thanks to that,
everything's settled now, isn't it?

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.170
Yes, no need to worry.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:34.580
Thanks to Ms. Owner and Andre's group,

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:37.130
the whole issue with the debt
is more or less settled.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:39.330
And I don't need to worry about
marrying anyone, either.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.960
Father and Caterina sent
their regards to everyone too.

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:45.380
Glad to hear it!

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:49.540
Well then, once we're done drinking this,
let's open up the shop.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:50.460
Yeah!

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.500
Welco...

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:59.000
Ah, Dad!

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.790
You sure are working hard.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:02.380
Are you on your way back from buying stock?

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.670
Yeah, and I was entrusted with
a letter for Sarasa.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.670
The Feed Company?

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.670
Ms. Sarasa's family...!

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:15.830
Alright...

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:20.290
These should not just be good for
blacksmiths, but for cooking too.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:21.790
Yes?

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:26.540
Sorry, I didn't want to bother you
while you're working, but...

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.080
From the Feed Company?

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:36.080
Ms. Sarasa Feed, apologies for
not contacting you all this time.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:39.500
I am the head clerk of
the Feed Company, Leroy.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:43.580
I heard from the head of the orphanage
that you were in Yok Village,

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.790
and so I sent this message to get in contact.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:47.960
The head clerk...

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:53.710
Allow me to get straight to my reason
for writing you this letter.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:04:01.330
Our Feed Corporation wishes to welcome you
back as the heir to the business, Sarasa.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:07.630
It's taken a long time since that
unforeseen incident seven years ago,

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:10.630
but we finally seem to be getting
the business back on track.

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:13.290
And so, I sent you this message.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:19.000
I would very much appreciate the opportunity
to talk with you in person at least once.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:23.380
This certainly is sudden.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:24.960
What do you think, Ms. Owner?

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:26.790
I'm not sure.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:30.790
Personally, I had thought all ties
between us had been cut.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.920
It's not the sort of thing
you need to rush into.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.460
Why not think it out calmly
until you can sort it all out?

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:43.420
Right.

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:46.000
Yes, that's just what I'll do.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:55.210
When are you going to be back?

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:59.170
We don't have too much to transport,
so we should be back by dusk.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:00.670
Be a good girl and wait for us, okay?

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:02.250
Well then, we're off!

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.130
Take care!

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.960
Mom, Dad!

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:18.960
What's the matter?

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:23.130
I'll make sure to watch over the shop
while you're away!

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.500
We're counting on you.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:27.790
After all, the place will be
all yours in the future.

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:28.750
Yeah!

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:32.040
And I'll make it even bigger, too!

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:45.290
Lorea,

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:47.250
I'm going out for a bit.

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:49.960
Wh-where to?

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:52.040
Just for a bit of a change of pace.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.710
I've been holed up in my workshop
for a while, after all.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:56.420
Will you be back soon?

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:57.420
Hmm?

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.710
I'll be back before dinner.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.750
Got it.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.500
I'm off.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:06.580
Take care.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:20.670
Good afternoon, Mrs. Elles, Mr. Jasper!

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.540
Hey there, Sarasa!

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.460
What brings you our way today?

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:26.460
I'm just out for a bit of a stroll.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:28.960
Sounds great!

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:32.580
Um, would you care to join me...?

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:38.330
Sorry for the sudden request.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.880
Feel free to do it day in and day out!

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:45.130
All I've got back home is my husband,
always making such difficult faces.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:52.040
By the way, how long has it been now
since you first came to the village?

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:53.580
Half a year.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.670
You went and showed me around
just like this back then.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:58.420
Yeah, that's right!

00:06:58.420 --> 00:07:01.710
I pegged you as a bit of the unreliable sort at first.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:04.040
What about now?

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.830
You're like a little queen!

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:09.080
Please, cut it out!

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.920
What are you all up to?

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:19.830
Good afternoon, Mr. Geberk,
Mr. Gizdo, and Ms. Elyn.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:20.710
Hey there.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:22.580
Elyn here had a request for us.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:26.830
I figured the craftsmen of the village
could work together to make something.

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:29.040
Ooh, what a great idea!

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:31.460
We're starting with
something simple to give it a try.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:33.380
How wonderful!

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:35.540
The idea actually came from my father.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:36.960
From the mayor?

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:38.000
Yes.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.880
The number of gatherers about has grown
and the village has been prospering,

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:42.670
so he seems to be all fired up.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:45.630
He said we can't just keep
relying on you all the time, Sarasa.

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:48.880
Wow, that's certainly unexpected.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:50.580
Yeah, considering our mayor.

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:55.210
Oh right, and there's also the reward
for that investigation from before.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:59.000
How about we make you a field
for herbs next to your shop?

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.630
We can throw in a caretaker, too.

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:02.130
A field for herbs?

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:05.670
Yeah. We'd need help figuring out
how to grow them,

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:09.380
but I figured that would be the most
helpful thing for your business.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.170
No good...?

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:16.420
Ah, no...

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:18.290
I'd really appreciate it!

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:20.330
Thank goodness! Then it's decided.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:23.000
I'm really looking forward to it!

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:26.380
We're here for a meal, Delal!

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:30.040
What, you're here to drink
in the middle of the day again?

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:33.170
Geez, is that all you can say?

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:34.380
Good afternoon.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.460
It sure has been a while, Sarasa!

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:40.580
Sorry. I've been so busy with the shop
I haven't been able to make my way over.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:45.580
Don't you worry. I mean, we've been
earning a ton here thanks to you.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.290
The stove has been working out great.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:53.420
Today's on the house, so eat up
to your heart's content, Sarasa!

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:54.830
Hooray!

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:59.000
Thanks for everything today.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.500
It was a ton of fun.

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:02.670
I mean, we got to talk a whole lot
for the first time in a while.

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:03.710
I enjoyed it too.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:08.670
I really am glad you came here to the village.

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:11.460
Everyone's so lively now compared to before.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:13.170
That's no exaggeration.

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:16.540
I'll keep on counting on you from here on out.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:17.420
Right!

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:32.750
Um, I'm thinking of heading to
the Feed Company!

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:38.670
Th-then, do you mean...

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:42.040
No, I haven't decided on
how to respond just yet.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:44.710
It's more that I want to head there
so I can make up my mind.

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:46.250
I-I see...

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:49.080
Since you won't know until you
talk to them directly, right?

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:52.330
Yes. So I have something to discuss
with all of you...

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:56.420
It takes half a month each way
to reach the capital.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:10:01.540
So thinking ahead, I'll be away
from the village for over a month.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.210
Could I ask you all to look after
the shop in the meantime?

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:09.170
O-of course! Just leave it to us!

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:12.960
Naturally. After all,
you've helped us out so much.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.710
Of course I'll pay the two of you
proper wages for your help.

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.630
You needn't worry about that.

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:19.500
I'll take it.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.830
Huh?! Ah, right...

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:26.330
I just got a little carried away there,
and let my emotions get the better of me.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:29.210
I'll make enough potions for
while I'm away in advance.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:31.830
And I already discussed
the matter of helping

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:35.170
with purchasing ingredients
with Ms. Leonora.

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:38.670
Could I ask Mr. Darna to help with
transporting everything again?

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:40.580
Right, I'll ask him.

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:44.420
You'll be the acting head of the shop
while I'm away, Lorea.

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:45.750
I will?!

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:48.750
I'll leave it to you two to determine
when you can help out.

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:49.460
Right.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:50.420
Understood.

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:54.920
You can already run the shop
without needing my guidance, Lorea.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.290
I'm sure you'll do just fine!

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:01.420
Got it! I'll give it my all!

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:07.580
Well then, please take care of the place.

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:08.750
Safe travels.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:09.830
Take care.

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:11.330
Leave the shop to us!

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:51.170
Is that you, Sarasa...?

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:54.750
Mister head clerk...

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:13.080
Sorry for making you come all this way.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:17.040
I was figuring we'd come get you
after getting in contact.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:18.170
Ah, no...

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:22.330
I'm sure the sudden message
caught you off guard.

00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:23.580
Naturally...

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:27.830
Did you figure we had
abandoned you all this time?

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:33.790
We had a lot of goods stolen in
the incident where we lost your parents.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:39.000
And so, the company was saddled with
greater debt than ever before.

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:43.830
Back then, we even considering
disbanding the company.

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:46.000
But after discussing the matter
among the management,

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:50.290
everyone wanted to keep your parents'
company that had helped us out going.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:55.540
We really did all want to look after you,
but we just couldn't stand

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:59.080
the thought of you seeing
the shop in such a state...

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:02.790
And so I asked the head of the orphanage
not to tell you anything

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:05.290
until the shop got back on its feet.

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:08.830
I fully understand if you don't believe me...

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:10.920
No, I understood.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:11.920
Huh?

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:16.330
I was of course sad at first,
but as I studied all sorts of things,

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:18.750
I figured it must have been
something like that.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:24.290
It took us seven years to reach this point.

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:28.710
I didn't come here because
I've made up my mind to return.

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:33.920
For now, I want to see how the shop my
father and mother left behind is being run.

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:35.290
I see...

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:40.130
We'll be waiting till you
come to a decision, Sarasa.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:41.500
Right.

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:44.170
Welcome!

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:47.170
Hey there!
Working hard, eh, acting owner?

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:48.630
Yes! I'm trying my best!

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:50.130
Could we ask you to buy these?

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:53.830
For the time being, we'll simply
hold on to them for you.

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:55.630
Right, no worries.

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:57.290
Where are Iris and Kate?

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:00.710
They're out gathering today,
so their skills don't grow too rusty.

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:01.750
I see.

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:04.920
Still, Sarasa still isn't back yet, huh?

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:07.000
Oww!

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.000
We told you not to say that!

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.460
Ow! Sorry!

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:14.080
W-well then, I'll have these appraised by

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:17.380
the alchemist coming from
South Straug next week.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:18.210
Got it!

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:19.290
Welcome!

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:22.790
I heard from my buddy that you
might have flexible gloves.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:25.460
We do! Please hold on just a moment.

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:28.630
You sure have gotten the hang of the job.

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:33.330
I wish I could handle
the purchases myself, though.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:37.000
Well, everybody's got things
they can do and things they can't.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:38.080
Give it your all!

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:38.920
Right!

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:42.830
Hey, Lorea...

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:46.500
Isn't this...

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:48.460
A bit much?

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:51.290
Since you didn't get all that much today,

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:54.000
you should eat a whole lot
and try hard again tomorrow.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:56.630
Yes, but still, this amount...

00:14:56.960 --> 00:15:00.130
You shouldn't slack off just because
Ms. Sarasa isn't around.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:04.170
Even without the marriage,
you still have your debt.

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:06.500
It's not like we've been slacking, though.

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:08.710
It just happened to be one of those days.

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:12.460
With that said, it's true that
I've been feeling discouraged.

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:13.580
Yeah...

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:15.000
Both of you...

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:18.210
Pull yourselves together!

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:24.040
Thank you so very much.

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:29.080
Those fruits from Osford you sold me
earned themselves quite a good reception!

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:31.130
I'd love to buy some more from you.

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:34.420
I'll introduce you to some more
great products from the region.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:37.500
That workshop you
introduced me to is fantastic!

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:41.710
The prices are low, so I can sell for
cheaper to my customers!

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.000
Do you mean it?!

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:47.040
The head of the place will be happy to hear
someone finally appreciates his work.

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:50.790
We always feel safe trusting you
with our luggage.

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:54.420
Yeah, since we put on more guards
than other places.

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:57.170
We take extra care on that front.

00:15:57.170 --> 00:16:00.460
A lot of folks out there can't keep on
living without these supplies,

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:02.460
so you're seriously lifesavers.

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:06.000
What do you think of the place?

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:08.750
It's a truly wonderful shop.

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:14.540
If you come back,
you could use your alchemy

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:18.710
to help bring prosperity and joy
to even more people.

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:24.710
We want you to carry on this shop
that your parents left behind,

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:27.330
and their philosophy towards business.

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:32.170
Could I have just a bit more time
to think on it?

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:34.920
Thank you!

00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:40.290
It sure has gotten busy lately, hasn't it?

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:43.420
It's probably because Mr. Andre's group
has been spreading around

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:46.710
the information Ms. Owner taught them
about various ingredients, right?

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:50.040
So that's why there are so many
unfamiliar gatherers around?

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:51.960
It may stay that way for a while.

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:54.330
Still, what awful timing...

00:16:55.710 --> 00:17:00.130
Come on, now! Let's get things ready
for tomorrow, then eat dinner!

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:11.040
We want you to carry on this shop
that your parents left behind,

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:13.710
and their philosophy towards business.

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:18.710
We're counting on you. After all,
the place will be all yours in the future.

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:19.670
Yeah!

00:17:19.670 --> 00:17:23.210
And I'll make it even bigger, too!

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:40.380
Good evening.

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:43.040
Welcome... Sarasa?!

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:45.790
Long time no see, Ms. Maria.

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:48.040
I had a bit of business here in the capital.

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:51.330
My, why didn't you let us know in advance?

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.750
Sorry...

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:55.290
Did something happen?

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:59.210
Well, er, how should I put it...?

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:04.330
She's in the workshop,
so go ahead and see her.

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:07.250
Master!

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:09.130
Ah, Sarasa.

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:11.580
You aren't surprised at all, are you?

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:14.830
What could be surprising about
an apprentice returning to her master?

00:18:14.830 --> 00:18:16.540
Yeah, but still...

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:18.960
Well, I know just why you came.

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:25.170
You're mad that I didn't lend a hand
in your battle with the salamander, right?

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:26.750
That was because I trusted in your skills...

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:28.040
Not even close.

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:28.830
Hmm?

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:32.250
Wait, so that really was you, huh, Master?

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.380
Thank you for coming along.

00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:37.460
I can't think of any other matters it could be.

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:39.500
Well you see...

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:42.670
I see.

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:46.750
It's true that I've heard plenty of talk
about the Feed Company,

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:49.460
but I never expected them
to welcome you back.

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:50.460
Right...

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:53.630
Alright, since you came all this way,

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:56.080
why don't I give you your first
sword lesson in a while?

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:57.000
Huh?!

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:04.420
But why...?

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:08.880
When you're worrying over something,
it's best to clear your head.

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:10.580
Really?

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:11.460
Here I come!

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:15.830
Sarasa, you're an outstanding apprentice.

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:20.670
Whether it comes to your sword skills,
your alchemy, or even your temperament.

00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:24.380
But you're too outstanding.

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:27.960
It's important to understand
how things should be done,

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:30.330
but you restrain yourself too much.

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:32.290
It's fine to be selfish every now and then.

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:39.630
You said your parents didn't run their
business solely to earn money, didn't you?

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:40.920
That's right.

00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:46.250
They aimed to run an honest business
that made everyone involved happy.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:50.960
So in that case...

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:55.130
The idea of running a business
that makes everyone involved happy...

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:59.540
I figure that "everyone"
needs to include you too.

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:07.040
Gotcha.

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:12.580
Welcome!

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:15.000
Please go ahead and buy all of this.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.040
My buddies told me this place
pays the highest,

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:19.420
so I gathered up everything
and brought it along.

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:22.580
I-it will take a bit for us
to appraise everything...

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:25.710
That won't do at all! I'm in a hurry!

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:27.830
Yes, but right now the owner is...

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:28.960
Excuse me.

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:31.750
Are these the only preserved foods
you have in stock?

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:34.170
Ah, I believe there should be
more somewhere...

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.710
Excuse me! My child was bit by a bug!

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:40.210
Do you have any potions that work on
swelling, itching, and fevers?!

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:42.080
Huh? A potion like that...

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:43.170
Please hurry!

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:44.880
Er! Umm...!

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:46.080
We do!

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:53.750
Ms. Sarasa!
Ms. Owner!

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:56.920
Ms. Iris, grab the green bottle
under the counter.

00:20:57.630 --> 00:20:59.960
Ms. Kate, the preserved goods

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:02.290
are on the third shelf from
the bottom in the workshop.

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:06.170
Lorea, I can handle
that amount right away.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:07.960
Ms. Sarasa...!

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:09.790
Ms. Owner!

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:11.330
Ms. Owner...!

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:13.040
I'm back!

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:18.580
Welcome home!

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:19.750
Ah, Lorea...!

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:21.790
Mish Sharasa!

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:24.580
I'm sorry for taking so long.

00:21:25.210 --> 00:21:28.040
Come on, now.
We mustn't make the customers wait.

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:29.790
Right!

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:34.880
You'll all be dealt with soon, everyone!

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:42.630
So this shop and the one from
your parents will be collaborating?

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:47.210
Well, we agreed to maintain a link
between us and share information,

00:21:47.210 --> 00:21:50.000
and we may have some
dealings of course too.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:52.710
And they accepted that right away?

00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:56.460
Yes, since I conveyed my feelings
to them properly.

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:58.540
Your feelings, Ms. Sarasa...?

00:21:58.830 --> 00:21:59.750
Yeah.

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:03.920
This shop really has turned into
a wonderful business

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:06.170
thanks to all your efforts.

00:22:06.580 --> 00:22:10.420
A fantastic place the lives up to
my father and mother's ideals.

00:22:11.920 --> 00:22:12.830
However...

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:15.250
Now I understand that

00:22:15.250 --> 00:22:18.880
in order to make everyone happy,
I need to make myself happy as well.

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:24.670
I want to develop my own shop
in Yok Village alongside everyone.

00:22:25.500 --> 00:22:28.460
And so, I can't work here.

00:22:30.290 --> 00:22:31.420
I see.

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:33.790
I really am sorry.

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:37.460
I wish I could have shown your parents
the fine young woman you've grown into.

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:41.830
You've become a wonderful manager.

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:45.540
I'm still a novice when it comes to
being an alchemist, though.

00:22:48.710 --> 00:22:54.500
Hajimete hiraku tobira sotto nozokeba

00:22:54.500 --> 00:23:02.040
Dokidoki ga tsunaideku takusan no egao

00:23:02.710 --> 00:23:09.630
Atarashii deai marugoto tsumekonde

00:23:09.630 --> 00:23:14.830
Majiwaru tabi umarete kuru harmony

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:21.880
Shinjitetai donna kanousei mo

00:23:21.880 --> 00:23:28.920
Kono sora ga asu mo mata harewataru you ni

00:23:29.170 --> 00:23:30.960
Thank you very much!

00:23:30.960 --> 00:23:32.580
Come back anytime!

00:23:37.460 --> 00:23:41.380
Labor costs:

00:23:37.460 --> 00:23:41.380
Transport fees:

00:23:37.460 --> 00:23:41.380
Salamander sales:

00:23:37.460 --> 00:23:41.380
Repayment of the house of Lotze's debt:
